WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.520
Growing up in a small Virginia town near the
mountains, right on the border of West Virginia,

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.430
Zane heard all kinds of stories from his grandmother.

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:12.210
Tales of mountain lions who could transform
into ghostly women.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:16.949
The tailypo, a fluffy rodent-like creature
on an endless quest to get its tail back from

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:18.619
the hunter who took it.

00:00:18.619 --> 00:00:23.640
The Mothman that appeared with glowing red
eyes to warn of impending tragedy.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.690
Most of all, she warned him about the deer.

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:31.191
"Sometimes," she used to say, "when you're
out in the woods late at night, you'll see

00:00:31.191 --> 00:00:33.640
a deer acting a little bit funny.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.900
Maybe it's making strange sounds.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.220
Maybe it's standing up like a man.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.230
Maybe it's staring at you from the shadows
and won't look away.

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:46.530
If you ever see one of these deer, promise
me you'll get away from it as fast as possible.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:50.310
Don't look at it, don't talk to it, just get
far, far away."

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:51.920
He promised her every time.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:56.920
But, as he got older, he started to forget
his grandma's stories, letting them fade away

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:00.280
with memories of the Easter Bunny and Santa
Claus.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:05.409
He didn't think about the stories again until
he was older, a junior in college, and embarking

00:01:05.409 --> 00:01:07.750
on a camping trip with his roommate, Josh.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:11.909
They were both staying with Zane's family
for the summer, and had been enjoying the

00:01:11.909 --> 00:01:14.189
sunshine and fresh air.

00:01:14.189 --> 00:01:18.829
They'd gone hiking, picked blackberries, and
gone fishing to their hearts' content.

00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:22.889
After a while, they got sick of sleeping in
the cramped house and decided to have a proper

00:01:22.889 --> 00:01:25.630
camping trip out in the mountains.

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:30.359
Campsites were crowded this time of year,
but Zane knew a spot just isolated enough

00:01:30.359 --> 00:01:34.630
that they could kick back, enjoy nature, and
relax in peace.

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:38.490
They packed their supplies and headed out
into the forest for a weekend they would never

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:39.490
forget.

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:43.630
By nightfall, Zane and Josh had pitched their
tents, built a fire, and were starting to

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:44.630
make some dinner.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:49.570
They roasted hot dogs and heated cans of beans
over the fire, and decided to start telling

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:52.079
some classic scary stories.

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:56.641
Sitting by the crackling fire, listening to
the rustling leaves, snapping twigs, and the

00:01:56.641 --> 00:02:01.789
chittering of animals all around, Zane couldn't
help but remember the stories he had almost

00:02:01.789 --> 00:02:02.799
forgotten.

00:02:02.799 --> 00:02:08.390
All of the strange, inexplicable things that
came out after the sun went down and the forest

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:09.390
went quiet.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:13.930
He thought he could hear the footsteps of
something walking by their campsite, circling

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:14.930
them.

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:17.000
But it was probably just his imagination.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.829
As Josh told stories about babysitters stalked
by killers and drivers picking up ghostly

00:02:21.829 --> 00:02:25.579
hitchhikers, Zane was thinking about the deer.

00:02:25.579 --> 00:02:30.719
He shuddered but shook it off, and after some
more stories and a few too many s'mores, the

00:02:30.719 --> 00:02:33.560
two friends decided to get some sleep.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:37.470
After several hours, Zane woke to the sound
of Josh unzipping his tent.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:41.890
He sat up, ready to yell at his friend for
waking him up, but the sight of Josh's pale,

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:43.760
frightened face stopped him.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:46.579
"There's something here..." was all Josh could
say.

00:02:46.579 --> 00:02:49.420
His hands, Zane noticed, were shaking.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:51.140
"Hey man, it's okay.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:54.040
Let's check it out," Zane patted Josh on the
shoulder.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.519
He was pretty sure his friend just wasn't
used to camping in actual nature, but reached

00:02:58.519 --> 00:03:00.790
for his hunting knife just in case.

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:05.569
He grabbed a flashlight, and switched it on,
following Josh out into the darkness.

00:03:05.569 --> 00:03:10.250
He swept the beam across the clearing, and
it illuminated a pair of orange eyes staring

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.109
directly at him from behind a nearby tree.

00:03:13.109 --> 00:03:17.499
"What the..." he approached the shape, trying
to get a clear look at it.

00:03:17.499 --> 00:03:20.900
As it became more illuminated, his stomach
dropped.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:24.890
It was a deer, but something was...wrong with
it.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:30.200
Its mouth was wide open, its jaw working up
and down like it was trying to make a sound,

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:31.340
but nothing came out.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:33.799
But that wasn't the worst part.

00:03:33.799 --> 00:03:39.639
As the flashlight beam illuminated the animal's
body, Zane realized that, somehow, its head

00:03:39.639 --> 00:03:41.299
was on backwards.

00:03:41.299 --> 00:03:44.819
"What the-" Josh appeared behind him, gasping.

00:03:44.819 --> 00:03:45.819
"Shh!"

00:03:45.819 --> 00:03:47.030
Zane shushed him intensely.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.090
He suddenly remembered his grandmother's warnings.

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:50.090
"You know what?

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:51.090
I don't feel so great.

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:53.310
I think we should go back to the car and head
to my place."

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:57.499
He gave Josh a look, shaking his head as if
to say "don't say another word."

00:03:57.499 --> 00:04:01.469
By the glow of their flashlights, the two
packed up their campsite, all under the gaze

00:04:01.469 --> 00:04:03.280
of the misshapen deer.

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:09.159
They drove home in silence, Josh only speaking
once to ask: "What was that thing?"

00:04:09.159 --> 00:04:10.189
Zane shook his head.

00:04:10.189 --> 00:04:11.299
"I don't know.

00:04:11.299 --> 00:04:12.359
But it wasn't a deer."

00:04:12.359 --> 00:04:15.219
They crept back into the house, and went to
bed.

00:04:15.219 --> 00:04:18.180
They knew they would never speak of tonight
ever again.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:23.470
As Zane began to drift off to sleep, his last
conscious thought was to glance out the window.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:27.710
There, in the yard not five feet away, was
a deer.

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:28.710
Watching.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:34.740
He didn't know it, but that night Zane encountered
an instance of SCP-6448.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:41.940
SCP-6448 is an anomalous species of creatures
that appear to belong to the Cervidae family,

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:44.080
nicknamed the "Not Deer."

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:49.509
They are highly intelligent and can be distinguished
from ordinary deer by unusual behavior and

00:04:49.509 --> 00:04:51.490
physical deformities.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:56.430
Some of these have included: legs that bend
backwards, the eyes of animals other than

00:04:56.430 --> 00:05:02.440
deer, forward-facing eyes, jerky movements,
lack of fear toward humans, and walking on

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:04.460
two hind legs.

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:11.509
Most notably, and most frightening, SCP-6448
instances will watch and stalk humans, for

00:05:11.509 --> 00:05:14.199
a duration of hours or even days.

00:05:14.199 --> 00:05:19.430
They will follow humans home, and steal items
from their domains including weapons, food,

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:20.840
and other personal items.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:25.800
They are most frequently found in the deep
woods at night, when a person is completely

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:26.800
alone.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:32.360
If someone encounters an instance of SCP-6448,
if they acknowledge any of the creature's

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:35.169
anomalous traits, it will attack.

00:05:35.169 --> 00:05:39.990
In order to limit the loss of life and ensure
that SCP Foundation employees exercise the

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:46.680
utmost caution when dealing with SCP-6448,
the Cryptozoology Division issued the following

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:47.680
guidelines:

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:52.280
"If you notice a deer that seems “off”,
look away and ignore it.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:55.449
If it knows that you’ve noticed it, it’s
too late.

00:05:55.449 --> 00:06:00.780
If you hear your name, whistling, or something
else in the woods calling for you, don’t

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.030
acknowledge it.

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:07.970
Never acknowledge it exists, don’t respond,
don’t go looking for it, don’t call back

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:08.970
to it.

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:12.360
If you’re walking at night and you feel
something breathing on your neck or whispering

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:17.479
behind you, the key to your safety is pretending
that everything is normal.

00:06:17.479 --> 00:06:21.060
Your survival is dependant on your ignorance."

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:28.490
Whatever SCP-6448 is, they appear to be intelligent
enough to understand when they are being studied,

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.199
and they don't seem to like it very much.

00:06:31.199 --> 00:06:40.039
On January 11, 1994, a group of three SCP-6448
instances broke into Site-41 in North Carolina,

00:06:40.039 --> 00:06:43.590
using a tunnel they had carved over a long
period of time.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:48.449
At that time, there was an instance in containment,
but in all of the chaos of the breach, the

00:06:48.449 --> 00:06:50.370
specimen was lost.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:56.750
Every time an instance was captured and contained
near SCP-6448's habitat, it would later escape

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:59.060
via similar tunnels.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:05.270
SCP-6448 was officially classified by the
SCP Foundation in 1980, but those from the

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:10.890
Appalachian region have known about these
strange creatures since at least 1947.

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:16.760
From folktales and campfire stories to secondhand
and even firsthand encounters, the locals

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:22.190
are well aware of the Not Deer's existence,
and are largely familiar with the precautions

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:24.259
necessary to avoid them.

00:07:24.259 --> 00:07:29.419
Though many of the civilians that encounter
SCP-6448 avoid notifying the authorities,

00:07:29.419 --> 00:07:35.449
there have been several recorded 911 calls
involving the Not Deer since 2000.

00:07:35.449 --> 00:07:38.139
The following is a log of those calls:

00:07:38.139 --> 00:07:40.040
February 1, 2000:

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:45.409
"Victim (aged 41, female) dialed emergency
services after hearing their name being called

00:07:45.409 --> 00:07:47.410
from the woods near their home.

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:51.569
The victim recounts the vocalization being
likened to a scream in a voice that they do

00:07:51.569 --> 00:07:56.719
not recognize and requested assistance in
locating the source.

00:07:56.719 --> 00:08:00.139
Emergency personnel requested the subject
place their phone on the floor outside the

00:08:00.139 --> 00:08:03.039
home to listen for the alleged sounds.

00:08:03.039 --> 00:08:08.110
After 2 minutes, a vocalization was heard
that was calling to the subject by name, emanating

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:10.050
from the nearby forest.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:11.050
&lrm;

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:14.430
The subject was instructed to investigate
the disturbance themselves and keep services

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.379
updated on the situation.

00:08:16.379 --> 00:08:21.259
The victim then begins to walk into the woodland,
getting about 50 meters into the underbrush

00:08:21.259 --> 00:08:23.569
before inexplicably stopping.

00:08:23.569 --> 00:08:28.289
They claim there to be a noticeably large
deer standing in the way of the path.

00:08:28.289 --> 00:08:32.340
She begins to walk closer, though states it
does not move.

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:35.880
Subject diverts from the path and begins walking
in a different direction.

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:39.390
After 30 minutes, no source of the voice is
determined.

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:41.950
The caller returns to their residence."

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.450
June 13, 2002:

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:48.590
"Victim (aged 28, male) calls 911 regarding
a home break-in.

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:54.610
The caller notes numerous items to be missing
from their residence and requests an investigation.

00:08:54.610 --> 00:09:00.780
Operators dispatch two investigators to visit
the home and pertain a potential perpetrator.

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:06.610
The pair note that, based on earlier CCTV
images, all cutlery, sharp objects, firearms,

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:11.740
lightbulbs, and a single copy of the novel
‘The Day After Roswell’ are missing.

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:16.040
Also noted is that there is a complete lack
of any fingerprints at the scene, with no

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:18.870
doors or windows having been broken into.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:24.660
Analysis of the home’s CCTV footage revealed
there to be a two hour period of missing film,

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:29.720
with the exception of a single frame containing
a Cervus nippon on its hind legs, reaching

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:31.170
towards the camera.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:34.330
Its frontal hooves have been warped to resemble
fingers.

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:37.710
No footage of the entity exiting the home
was discovered."

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:39.820
November 19, 2005:

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:44.950
"A cattle farmer (aged 54, male) reported
to local authorities the sudden disappearance

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:48.170
of over 30% of his largest herd.

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:52.920
Response teams searched the nearby area for
4 hours though found no trace of the cattle.

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:57.770
The victim was recommended to set up trail
cameras and note any unusual activity overnight.

00:09:57.770 --> 00:10:04.450
At 01:11 AM, two SCP-6448 are seen walking
through the field before fleeing.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:09.220
One places an object into the ground, later
discovered to be a single fork.

00:10:09.220 --> 00:10:14.900
A week after this discovery, 200 discarded
bovine hooves appear at the location."

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:16.780
March 4, 2009:

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:23.340
"Victim (age unknown, gender unknown) dials
911 to request assistance from animal services.

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:28.270
The victim is standing within a forest in
front of a Cervus elaphus, which is violently

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:29.270
contorting.

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:33.460
The victim attempts to state "You better get
a vet or something, I don't think it's well"

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:37.010
before a piercing screech is heard and the
line falls silent.

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:40.730
Recovered footage depicts the aforementioned
animal squirming, seemingly in pain.

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:46.770
A viscous churning is audible as a black mass
erupts out of the instance, and the video

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:48.340
turns to static."

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:50.220
October 11, 2012:

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:56.740
"Victim (aged 23, male) is a junior wildlife
officer at Cherokee National Forest, Tennessee.

00:10:56.740 --> 00:11:01.920
They radio their supervisor in the early evening
regarding a herd of Odocoileus virginianus

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:03.410
within the reserve.

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:08.331
Supposedly, there is a single animal that,
upon first glance, appears average, though

00:11:08.331 --> 00:11:14.570
possesses divergent attributes, including
backwards joints, enlarged abdomen, and forward-facing

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:15.600
eyes.

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:19.950
Upon stating this, a distant whistle is audible,
and the victim stumbles slightly.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:23.740
They begin to say “What the he- did it just
whistle at me?”

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:26.930
before the sound of hooves rapidly getting
closer is heard.

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:31.630
Notably, the hoof steps did not sound to be
in the traditional gallop of a cervid."

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:33.620
October 12, 2012:

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:38.230
"The former victim’s supervisor calls authorities
following the victim’s absence from the

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:40.100
reserve night shift.

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:42.250
Following this, their radio begins to crackle.

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:47.529
The victim’s voice can be heard on the other
end, and he requests the supervisor’s attention.

00:11:47.529 --> 00:11:51.750
&lrm; &lrm; He calls regarding a herd of Odocoileus
virginianus within the reserve.

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:56.710
They claim there is a single animal that upon
first glance appears average, though possesses

00:11:56.710 --> 00:12:03.350
divergent attributes including backwards joints,
enlarged abdomen and forward facing eyes.

00:12:03.350 --> 00:12:07.600
Suspecting the creature to be a rare genetic
malformation, the victim requests their supervisor

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:09.649
to come to the location.

00:12:09.649 --> 00:12:13.360
The supervisor questions the victim about
what happened the night previous.

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:14.420
There is no reply.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:19.480
Upon the supervisor’s and law enforcement’s
arrival at the site, a herd of approximately

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:22.200
80 Odocoileus virginianus was present.

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:26.410
A single entity is in the field’s center
and appears to be standing separate from the

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:27.640
rest of the group.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:31.240
It flees the scene upon realizing the law
enforcement’s presence.

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:34.120
Where it formerly stood laid a standard two-way
radio."

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:36.280
April 8, 2016:

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:42.030
“Victim (aged 35, female) dials 911 using
a satellite phone, distressed.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:46.510
They state that they are in [REDACTED] County
Woods and are being followed.

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:51.430
She claims that, despite seeing no one for
the duration of her hike, she “feels as

00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:55.890
if she’s being watched” and has heard
someone walking behind her at various points

00:12:55.890 --> 00:12:56.920
in the trip.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:13:01.370
The victim is unable to give an adequate description
of their location, but knows the route to

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:03.540
return to her residence.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:07.220
Operators request the victim to return to
a point wherein she can provide a sufficient

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:09.600
geographic description of her position.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:13.440
&lrm; The victim remains on the line for the
duration of the hike back to a readily used

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:15.510
portion of the wilderness trail.

00:13:15.510 --> 00:13:19.150
Along the journey, various unnatural sounds
can be heard.

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:24.240
These include footsteps, rockslides, coughing,
whispering, and whistling.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:29.150
Nearing the main trail, all woodland noises,
such as birds and wind, cease suddenly, and

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:33.860
the victim states she can see a malformed
deer carcass coated in a thick layer of black

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:34.860
slime.

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:38.290
At this time, human screams can be heard in
the distance.

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:42.080
Operators request the victim continue and
ignore other stimuli.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:48.050
Agents embedded in local law enforcement,
suspecting SCP-6448 involvement, notify Gamma-4

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:49.050
to the situation.

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:53.060
20 minutes later, the victim returns to the
main trail.

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:58.130
Gamma-4, now operating the 911 call, informs
the victim not to respond to any further unusual

00:13:58.130 --> 00:14:01.640
activity and briefly outlines Cervus Protocol.

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:06.330
For the duration of the victim’s journey
to her home, two sets of breathing are audible.

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:10.540
The victim successfully returns to her residence
and shuts the door behind her.

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:16.100
Now out of sight from SCP-6448, agents inquire
at the victim’s address, and the victim

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:17.990
promptly complies.

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:21.810
Operatives instruct the victim to have possession
of all firearms and weapons on the premises

00:14:21.810 --> 00:14:26.180
and to barricade herself inside a safe space
with one exit point.

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:31.240
The victim swiftly begins grabbing all available
weapons and throwing them inside a wardrobe.

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:34.110
It is at this time that there is a knock on
the front door.

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:38.930
The victim does not respond and continues
to hoard sharp objects from kitchen drawers.

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:43.150
The knocking becomes more violent as the handle
is jostled and shaken incessantly.

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:48.360
A voice on the other side repeats the phrase
“Hello, it is me.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:50.230
Hello, let me in.”

00:14:50.230 --> 00:14:53.110
in a calm manner as the door begins to shake.

00:14:53.110 --> 00:14:56.970
The victim retreats to her wardrobe, armed
with a small firearm.

00:14:56.970 --> 00:15:01.570
Upon sealing herself in the space, the knocking
ceases, and footsteps can be heard becoming

00:15:01.570 --> 00:15:02.910
further away.

00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:06.200
The sound of galloping is audible as the front
door caves in.

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:09.350
Hoof steps can now be heard inside the home.

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:13.140
The entity continues to repeat “Hello, it
is me.

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:14.870
Hello, let me in.”

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:16.750
as it searches the small building.

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:20.260
A bright light flashes overhead, seemingly
circling the house.

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:23.000
Eventually, the entity enters the victim’s
bedroom.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:28.480
Through a small slit in the wardrobe door,
the victim can see a Cervus canadensis standing

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:31.440
on its hind legs and surveying the room.

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:36.910
Its movements are crooked and stiff, seeming
to struggle to stand in a bipedal fashion.

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:42.000
It slouches down to a quadrupedal crouch,
similar to the stance of an arachnid.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:46.220
It inhales heavily, and its head locks on
the view of the wardrobe.

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:48.720
It is noted as possessing human eyes.

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:51.370
It scampers towards the subject and opens
the door.

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:53.580
A single gunshot is heard.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:58.860
Responders found no trace of either SCP-6448
or the victim."

00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:03.810
Containment of SCP-6448 is focused on the
investigation of any deer exhibiting anomalous

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:07.170
traits in and around the Appalachian area.

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:13.170
Any civilian sightings of SCP-6888 are to
be handled by Mobile Task Force Gamma-4, or

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:14.980
the "Green Stags".

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:20.740
Any possible deaths resulting from SCP-6448
will be blamed on hiking accidents, and any

00:16:20.740 --> 00:16:24.680
reported sightings can be explained away with
Chronic Wasting Disease.

00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:30.670
CWD, occasionally referred to as "zombie deer
disease" is a prion disease affecting members

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:32.570
of the Cervidae family.

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:37.500
Symptoms of the illness include loss of motor
function control and damage to decision making,

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:41.070
as well as gradual degradation of all mental
faculties.

00:16:41.070 --> 00:16:43.340
It is one hundred percent fatal.

00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:48.750
However, though the disease does exist, most
recorded cases of it in the Appalachian region

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:53.730
can actually be attributed to instances of
SCP-6448.

00:16:53.730 --> 00:17:00.890
Any captured instances of SCP-6448 should
be transported to Site-44 for the Cryptozoology

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:02.950
Division's containment and study.

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:09.890
On November 29, 2019, they finally got their
chance to bring a Not Deer into custody.

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:15.629
The Green Stags were able to capture an instance
of SCP-6448 with help from MTF Nu-7, "Hammer

00:17:15.629 --> 00:17:21.939
Down", and their heavy vehicles division,
as well as some experimental shock rifles.

00:17:21.939 --> 00:17:26.589
One Not Deer was knocked unconscious in the
conflict, and its body was loaded onto an

00:17:26.589 --> 00:17:31.370
armored helicopter and flown straight to Site-44
in Essex, England.

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:36.929
At the site, it was then placed in a reinforced
steel containment cell, and heavily sedated.

00:17:36.929 --> 00:17:39.379
This entire process went off without a hitch.

00:17:39.379 --> 00:17:44.750
As the entity began to regain consciousness,
Cryptozoology Specialist F. Ozz watched it

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:49.539
through a one-way glass window and attempted
to speak to it through the intercom.

00:17:49.539 --> 00:17:53.559
"Greetings, SCP-6448," Researcher Ozz began.

00:17:53.559 --> 00:17:57.340
At the sound of his voice, the creature jumped
to its feet, staring at the intercom.

00:17:57.340 --> 00:17:59.429
"Can you understand me?

00:17:59.429 --> 00:18:02.529
We've seen your genus speak English just fine
in the past."

00:18:02.529 --> 00:18:06.770
The animal did not answer, but began licking
one of its legs and behaving as if it were

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:08.610
an ordinary deer.

00:18:08.610 --> 00:18:10.240
Researcher Ozz sighed impatiently.

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:12.370
"Please, we know your secret."

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:17.610
The Not Deer stopped what it was doing, freezing
completely still as it listened to his words.

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:20.059
"Admittedly, it wasn't exactly well kept.

00:18:20.059 --> 00:18:23.970
If you'd just look at yourself for more than
a few seconds, it is very clear that you're

00:18:23.970 --> 00:18:25.659
not...normal."

00:18:25.659 --> 00:18:30.980
At this, the creature, which had been facing
away from the window, swiveled its neck 180

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:33.600
degrees, breaking its own spine with an audible
crack.

00:18:33.600 --> 00:18:38.299
It stared, unblinking, at the window and directly
at Researcher Ozz.

00:18:38.299 --> 00:18:41.200
Ozz turned to the containment staff, suddenly
anxious.

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.960
"I thought you said this was one-way?"

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:48.789
The staff assured him that it was, and there
was no way the Not Deer could see him.

00:18:48.789 --> 00:18:51.830
Still, its eyes were locked directly on his
face.

00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:55.320
He shook off the sense of unease and continued
his line of questioning.

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:58.059
"Are you something imitating deer?

00:18:58.059 --> 00:19:02.549
It is clear that, if so, you possess basic
anatomical knowledge of them, though details

00:19:02.549 --> 00:19:03.659
are clearly faulty.

00:19:03.659 --> 00:19:05.830
In fact, a better question would be...how?

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:09.789
If, in fact, you are not what you pretend
to be."

00:19:09.789 --> 00:19:14.269
The Not Deer opened its mouth at this, revealing
unusually sharp teeth.

00:19:14.269 --> 00:19:19.070
It moved its jaw as if attempting to speak,
but only a choking sound came out.

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:21.460
"Shall we move on?"

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:22.460
Ozz asked.

00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:25.649
"What I'm more concerned with here is why
you take our people.

00:19:25.649 --> 00:19:26.649
Is it a vendetta?

00:19:26.649 --> 00:19:27.649
Spite?

00:19:27.649 --> 00:19:28.649
Food?"

00:19:28.649 --> 00:19:31.200
For the first time in the interview, the Not
Deer blinked.

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:36.700
It was an unnatural movement, forced and deliberate,
like the creature was attempting to engage

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:42.170
in an ordinary behavior rather than actually
experiencing an involuntary impulse.

00:19:42.170 --> 00:19:45.840
"Responding is mandatory," Researcher Ozz
prompted.

00:19:45.840 --> 00:19:47.340
The creature did not react.

00:19:47.340 --> 00:19:51.029
"If you will not comply," Ozz's tone grew
stern, frustrated.

00:19:51.029 --> 00:19:54.659
"Maybe you'd like to see your brand new containment
cell."

00:19:54.659 --> 00:19:59.000
At last, the entity spoke.

00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:01.980
"R-Rasaerch.

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:04.960
Research."

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:08.200
Its voice resembled a distorted version of
Ozz's.

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:09.299
"Research?

00:20:09.299 --> 00:20:10.840
What kind of..."

00:20:10.840 --> 00:20:13.490
Ozz wasn't able to finish his question.

00:20:13.490 --> 00:20:19.270
"July 7, 1947," the creature said, before
ramming into the one-way glass and cracking

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:20.270
it.

00:20:20.270 --> 00:20:24.350
As Ozz stumbled backward from the force, the
creature collapsed on the ground, seizing

00:20:24.350 --> 00:20:25.770
and screaming as its abdomen.

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:27.620
"Get the Stags in here now!"

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:29.950
Ozz cried out, but it was too late.

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:34.799
A black mass of something shiny and tendriled
leaped out of the Not Deer, scuttling around

00:20:34.799 --> 00:20:39.679
the cell before shattering the window and
leaving the empty shell of a deer behind.

00:20:39.679 --> 00:20:45.409
The Site-44 Breach System activated and attempted
to initiate emergency containment protocols,

00:20:45.409 --> 00:20:50.580
but the mysterious black mass escaped its
sector, made its way toward the main exit,

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:55.830
broke through the glass on the front exit
door, and vanished into the shrubbery outside.

00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:59.029
The escaped anomaly could not be found and
recontained.

00:20:59.029 --> 00:21:02.740
Ever since this incident, there have been
a record-breaking number of Chronic Wasting

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:08.620
Disease cases identified in deer in the surrounding
area, as well as an unprecedented increase

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:10.620
in UFO reports.

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:15.179
Further research is currently ongoing, but
it is unknown whether we will ever truly know

00:21:15.179 --> 00:21:17.159
what these creatures are.

00:21:17.159 --> 00:21:22.240
Only one thing is for certain: they are definitely
not deer.

00:21:22.240 --> 00:21:29.081
Now go check out “SCP-966 - Sleep Killer”
and “SCP-2571 - Cragglewood Park” for

00:21:29.081 --> 00:21:32.269
more anomalies that’ll ensure you’ll never
want to sleep again!

00:21:32.269 --> 00:21:33.590
Wait, is that a deer behind you?

00:21:33.590 --> 00:21:33.601
Oh, god--

